From: IrfanMohammad <irfan@graphiant.com>
Date: Sun, 30 Jul 2023 19:42:14 +0000
Subject: fix skip predicate

predicate skip is poorly written. It does not account for predicates
containing quotes. for example [name="O'Brien"] or [secret ='n53l"LF8D']

Also add tests for it.
Add gnmi test yang modules to sysrepo for simpler debugging in future.
---
 src/common.c                           |   2 +-
 tests/files/gnmi-server-test-wine.yang |  38 +++++++++++
 tests/files/gnmi-server-test.yang      | 119 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 tests/test_oper_edit.c                 |  56 ++++++++++++++++
 4 files changed, 214 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)
 create mode 100644 tests/files/gnmi-server-test-wine.yang
 create mode 100644 tests/files/gnmi-server-test.yang

diff --git a/src/common.c b/src/common.c
index b130318..6231025 100644
--- a/src/common.c
+++ b/src/common.c
@@ -5009,7 +5009,7 @@ sr_xpath_skip_predicate(const char *xpath)
         } else if (!quot && ((xpath[0] == '\'') || (xpath[0] == '\"'))) {
             quot = xpath[0];
         }
-    } while (quot || (xpath[0] != ']'));
+    } while (xpath[0] && ( quot || (xpath[0] != ']')));
 
     return xpath + 1;
 }
